## General Problem-Solving Heuristics

<memory_item>
<description>
For "insert operators" problems, always verify candidate solutions by manual step-by-step evaluation respecting operator precedence, not just by trusting the expression at a glance. When multiple solutions exist (common for small targets with many operands), any valid solution is acceptable—select one and verify it. Brute-force enumeration is reliable and fast (4^n combinations) and should be used to confirm the heuristic's prediction. (Reference: Q1, Q2, Q3, Q5)
</description>
<example>
For 15 ? 19 ? 8 ? 2 ? 24 = 42, brute-force found 12 solutions. Verified 15 + 19 - 8 * 2 + 24 = 42 manually: 8*2=16, 15+19=34, 34-16=18, 18+24=42. ✓
</example>
</memory_item>
