## Optimization Techniques & Edge Cases

<memory_item>
<description>
Edge case: Division operations can produce floating-point results. When comparing to an integer target, use a tolerance (abs(result - target) < 1e-9) rather than exact equality to avoid floating-point representation errors. Also, division by zero raises ZeroDivisionError—always guard against it in brute-force loops. (Reference: Q1, Q2, Q5)
</description>
<example>
```python
try:
    result = eval(expr)
    if abs(result - target) < 1e-9:
        solutions.append((expr, result))
except ZeroDivisionError:
    continue
```
</example>
</memory_item>
